  "prefLabel": "Saf-C 3204.01 Applicant",
  "priorExpiration": "2016-01-12",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Saf-C 3204.01 Applicant.\n\n(a) An applicant for an inspection station shall be the owner of the business, or in the case of a corporation, partnership or other legal entity, a person with specific written authorization to sign the application.\n\n(b) The applicant shall be 18 years of age or older.\n\n(c) An applicant for a fleet inspection station shall own or lease at least 15 New Hampshire registered vehicles required to be inspected. Copies of all lease agreements shall be provided to the department, upon request.\n\nSource. (See Revision Notes at Chapter Heading Saf-C 3200) #8915, eff 6-22-07, EXPIRED: 6-22-15\n\nNew. #10886, INTERIM, eff 7-16-15, EXPIRES: 1-12-16; ss by #11016, eff 1-6-16",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/saf-c3200.html"
